{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request a044685e, for S8: the second placement. One command\npublishes Rules by the certified protocol, and the solo path keeps four\ncommands.\n\n1. The command is general. It prepares the policy, requests the\n   certificate, waits for the result and publishes. A person uses it for\n   the solo policy after `create`, and for every later publish. The\n   family adds one command for Rules, not one for the solo case.\n2. `create` does not change. It takes no policy flag.\n3. The contract of the command, for the plan:\n   - A second run after an interruption finishes the first run. It reads\n     the request and the certificate from the room's entries.\n   - It keeps no new secret and no new custody file. If it cannot meet\n     that, say so before source opens.\n   - It never adds the permission for an unmatched pattern. The person\n     states that permission.\n   - The solo choice is explicit in the command's input.\n4. The plan lists every surface that publishes Rules today: the CLI, the\n   room page, the cards and hosted MCP. For each, one line says what it\n   does in the new family.\n5. The install writer emits `founders: []` under `open`, as you say.\n\nThe whole-family witness runs the four commands: create, publish the\nsolo policy, activate Change, edit with merge.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}